    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working on my lit review and im stuck on citation stuff. if a paper has like 5 or 6 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for apa 7th vs chicago? i always get them mixed up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a paper with five or six authors, the difference between APA 7th and Chicago style is quite noticeable. In APA 7th, you'll use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" for every citation, even the first one. In Chicago style, depending on whether you're using notes-bibliography or author-date, you'll generally list the first author followed by \"et al.\" after the first citation, but the rules can be a bit more nuanced depending on the specific format you choose. It's always best to check the specific style guide for the nuances of your assignment.",
